Our fiscal year ends on the Sunday closest to August 31. References to the first quarter of 2025 and 2024 relate to the 12-week fiscal quarters ended November 24, 2024, and November 26, 2023. Certain percentages presented are calculated using actual results prior to rounding.
Highlights for the first quarter of 2025 versus 2024 include:
•Net sales increased 8% to $60,985, driven by an increase in comparable sales and sales at 26 net new warehouses opened since the end of the first quarter of 2024;
•Membership fee revenue increased 8% to $1,166, driven by new member sign-ups and upgrades to Executive Membership;
•Gross margin percentage increased 24 basis points; seven basis points excluding the impact of gasoline price deflation on net sales;
•SG&A expenses as a percentage of net sales increased 14 basis points and was flat excluding the impact of gasoline price deflation;

